# SwimAI — Project Rules

## Stack
- Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
- Package manager: pnpm only. Never suggest npm/yarn commands or generate package-lock.json/yarn.lock.
- Icons: lucide-react only.

## Content & i18n
- NEVER hardcode user-visible strings directly in JSX. All copy must come from
  i18n translation files (messages/en.json, messages/fr.json) via next-intl's
  useTranslations() hook, once i18n is set up.
- Until i18n is fully wired, the single source of truth for copy is lib/content.ts.
  Do not introduce a second source of truth — if new copy is needed, add it there first.
- French is the primary/default locale. English is secondary. Every new string
  added to fr.json must have a matching key added to en.json in the same change.
- Never invent translations silently — if unsure of an English phrasing, flag it
  rather than guessing.

## Components
- One component = one file, PascalCase filename matching the default export.
- Functional components only, typed props via an explicit `interface` (not inline
  object types), e.g. `interface CoachCardProps { coach: Coach }`.
- No inline `style={{...}}` objects except for things Tailwind genuinely cannot
  express (e.g. dynamic background-image URLs, gradient stops with alpha values).
  Everything else must use Tailwind utility classes.
- No raw hex colors in JSX/CSS. All colors must reference the design tokens
  defined in tailwind.config.ts (bg-deep, bg-navy, bg-panel, accent-teal,
  accent-blue, text-secondary, star-gold). If a new color is genuinely needed,
  add it to tailwind.config.ts first, then reference the token — never inline
  a hex value in a component.
- Shared types (Coach, NavLink, etc.) live in /types, never re-declared inline
  in multiple components.

## Routing
- Every <Link> or button that implies navigation must point to a real route —
  never href="#" or an empty onClick. If the destination page doesn't exist yet,
  create a minimal stub page rather than leaving a dead link.
- Routes follow the locale-prefixed structure once i18n is added: /[locale]/page-name.

## Images
- All raster images go through next/image (<Image />) with explicit width,
  height, and alt text — never a bare <img> tag.
- Decorative/background images that must be CSS background-image (not <Image />)
  should be marked aria-hidden="true" and use the optimized WebP version of the
  asset (not PNG/JPG) — see public/underwater-hero.webp as the existing pattern.
- New image assets must be compressed/converted to WebP before being added to
  /public. Flag any asset over ~200KB for review before committing.

## Accessibility
- Semantic HTML required: <header>, <nav>, <main>, <section>, <footer> — not
  generic <div> soup for structural elements.
- All interactive elements must be keyboard-reachable and have visible focus states.
- Decorative-only elements (background images, icon-only flourishes) get
  aria-hidden="true".

## General
- Before adding a new dependency, check if shadcn/ui, lucide-react, or an
  existing util already covers the need.
- Run `pnpm build` locally before considering a feature "done" — it must build
  with zero errors.